  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal Express has $75.4M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Federal Express won 175 awards so far, with an average award size of $431K. Federal Express obligations are down 80.6% year over year. Federal Express obligations peaked at $677M in FY24 and then moved to $582M in FY25, $388M in FY26, and $75.4M in FY27. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer for Federal Express in FY2027 to date, obligating $74.9M. The Department of Justice and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration follow at $124K and $121K respectively. Federal Express market activity in FY2027 to date is concentrated in Couriers and Express Delivery Services at $75.4M. The General Freight Trucking, Long-Distance, Less Than Truckload market shows $850. The FY2027 totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date obligations. This snapshot highlights current-year concentration by agency and industry and the drop in obligations compared with the prior year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Federal Express obligations changed year over year?",
        "body": "Federal Express obligations fell 80.6% year over year. Federal Express obligations by fiscal year show $309M in FY22, $275M in FY23, $677M in FY24, $582M in FY25, $388M in FY26, and $75.4M in FY27. The FY2027 total is partial, fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main federal buyers of Federal Express in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $74.9M for Federal Express in FY2027 to date. The Department of Justice obligated $124K and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $121K. Other buyers include the Department of the Treasury at $83.3K, the Department of Transportation at $40.8K, and smaller obligations from other agencies."
      }
    ]
  },
